Route W4A16 GEMMs on RDNA3 (ROCm, bf16): 1-4 rows to a single-read GEMV, 5-32 rows to a single-read WMMA kernel,
1024+ rows to dequant + hipBLASLt.

gptq_gemm_rdna3 reads the weights once per 4 activation rows, so a 5-row speculative verify reads them twice
and its inner loop spends ~2 FMAs per row and weight. rocm/w4a16_gemv.cu reads each weight word once for up to
8 rows on the same weight layout. One layer on a 7900 XTX, us per call, M=4 / M=5: gate_up 141 / 221 -> 121 / 125,
down 86 / 125 -> 64 / 67, o 37 / 47 -> 19 / 22. For prefill chunks (1024+ rows) the GEMM is compute-bound and
hipBLASLt bf16 beats gptq_gemm_rdna3: the same file dequantizes the layer to bf16 and the GEMM runs through torch,
~10% faster on the layer GEMMs at 1024-2048 rows. Optional: without /opt/hq/w4a16_gemv.so (built by
rocm/build_gemv.py), with HQ_W4A16_GEMV=0 or with fp16 activations the original kernel runs;
HQ_W4A16_DQ_MIN_M=0 turns the prefill path off.

The WMMA kernel (rocm/w4a16_gemv.cu, w4a16_wmma) covers 5-32 rows: one layer, us per call at M=16, gate_up 263 -> 131,
down 192 -> 83, qkv 77 -> 48, o 64 -> 38; at M=32 gate_up 510 -> 206 (weights read once instead of twice).
HQ_W4A16_WMMA=0 turns it off, HQ_W4A16_WMMA_MIN_M moves the GEMV/WMMA switch (default: WMMA above 4 rows).

